\ls1\ilvl0\cf3 {\listtext	1.	}My name is Nadia Zahmoul and I have become a target of 
\f2\i\b Kenes Rakishev
\f1\i0\b0 .\
{\listtext	2.	}He appointed Mr. Zahmoul to the Board of Directors of Oxus, a SPAC which is he controls.\
{\listtext	3.	}There are ongoing divorce proceedings in High Court since 2020 (case BV20D01752). The Final Hearing was on 19
\fs26\fsmilli13333 \super th
\fs32 \nosupersub  to 28
\fs26\fsmilli13333 \super th
\fs32 \nosupersub  of February 2024.\
{\listtext	4.	}Mr. Zahmoul made several false representations regarding Oxus under oath during cross-examination and directed his counsel to do the same. He also made false representations regarding the value of the Oxus shares on the asset schedule he filed on 19 February 2024.\
{\listtext	5.	}I wrote to the judge on 7 March 2024 to inform him of the false representations as this was material evidence. I wrote the judge again on 9 April 2024 with additional information regarding Mr. Zahmoul\'92s role within 
\f2\i\b Rakishev\'92s
\f1\i0\b0  inner circle.\
{\listtext	6.	}The judge sent the draft judgement to counsels on 9 April 2024.\
{\listtext	7.	}I am asserting that the judgment is significantly inconsistent with the evidence and the submissions presented during the Final Hearing which include: (i) the audio recordings of the Final Hearing, (ii) the court transcripts and attendance notes, (iii) the 6,000-page court bundle, counsel submissions and case statements.\
{\listtext	8.	}I am not qualified to draw any conclusions from my analysis, and I do not have a background in law. However, I am certain beyond doubt that the draft judgement in its content and tone is materially disconnected from and inconsistent with the facts and the evidence presented during the Final Hearing. Moreover, the draft judgement is inconsistent with the judge\'92s perception of the individual parties\'92 truthfulness, honesty, and moral standing as per his own non-verbal cues. This is a case where the entire strategy of my barrister was to demonstrate that Mr. Zahmoul is dishonest, morally corrupt, malevolent, and made significant non-disclosures. The cross examination was successful in demonstrating this. Mr. Zahmoul\'92s replies are on the record. \
{\listtext	9.	}While my assertions may seem aggressive, I would not have taken this course of action if my assertions could not be capable of being independently verifiable. Therefore, I am taking this risk because the outcome is unambiguous. The documentary evidence and court transcripts are available \ul through the link below\ulnone  to verify the facts and the audio recordings would have captured non-verbal cues, providing additional information on his character.\
