{\listtext	11.	}If my assertions regarding the draft judgement are corroborated, then 
\f2\i\b Rakishev\'92s
\f1\i0\b0  transnational reach is chilling, and the consequences are immense for us, for the nation\'92s security, and for the integrity of the democratic process. \
{\listtext	12.	}The judgement will be handed down today, 18 April 2024 and the court is aware that I do not have a barrister to assist me with the judgement and with my application to appeal the judgement.\
{\listtext	13.	}During the proceedings, I uncovered significant evidence of illicit activities and misconduct incriminating Mr. Zahmoul. The evidence was submitted in the court bundle at the Final Hearing, and I provided further evidence in cross examination.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl480\qj\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\i\b \cf3 {\listtext	14.	}Rakishev
\f1\i0\b0  has undertaken an aggressive 
\f2\i\b Reputation Laundering
\f1\i0\b0  campaign because he knows there is limited risk to his acts, and it served his best interest. This incentivised him to proceed with the 
\f2\i\b Reputation Laundering
\f1\i0\b0  campaign in order to protect the value of his intangible asset, which is Mr. Zahmoul\'92s 
\f2\i\b reputation
